 had Except y* Army there have some to spare according to y* Lords Justices Orders and Instructions w*^ I sent downe Lately to y*" High Sheriff w""^ I directed him to Communicate to you & y* Best of y« officers of y* Citty. Amunition is ordered for you; And you must Make y* best shift you can till Armes May be had. 50 of y' Army will be left in y* Towne to assist you w'** is all I could get or y* y* Gen" would spare. ^' I have a Com'' off oyer & Termin' putting under y* Seall impowering y* Justices off Peace or any 5 of them to try all the Rogues and Baparees y^ now are or hereafter shall be taken and to Hang such as deserve it, Soe y* will Cleare y* Goalls. '* There are orders Issuing to y* Adiacentt Countys viz Catherlow^ Watterford, Queens County & County Tiperrary to Joyne w'^ y* County Kilkenny in posting y* Militia of y' Respective Countys in y* best places for y* Defence thereof. It must be Every bodys best care and all Little Enough to defend y* Country where wee are Martched, for I feare the Baparees will Make it there bisiness to burne pillage & destroye y* Coun- try ; if any Armes doe come over I shall have my Share ; but I heare there are none yet come and y* Gen" is Soe hastty to take y' field y' he will not stay for any thing, & indeed he is in y* Right of itt for if wee can get uppon them before Succors comes w*"*" they Expect, they must be distroyed. " Give my Service to j' Son Warren & tell him y* y® Com" he has all- redy dose Intitle him to doe as much as what was Expressed in y* paper he Sent me by my L* And there will be a Com*' off oyer & Termin' to backe it; as any thing Matteriall offers pray let me here from you. I am " Yo' Assured friend & Serv* "Rich: Coote."* I Richard Coote, Esq., was one of hisMajesty'sdeclaratioDtinthecityand eight Justices appointed on the 24th connty of Kilkenny. — Walter Harris* July, 1690, to receive their arms and "Life and Reign" of King William, submission firom such as submitted to Appendix, p. Ixv. 253 '* Cap^ S^ George was w^ me to have Able Bottler, now Com^ to Cap^ Bnran, to be Cap^ warrons LS and Cap^ Bryan writt to me to j* same Effect, but I cannot See how j* can be done Except Egar is willing to Resigne, or some Ezch ^.** The ensuinff document is what would now be termed a copy of the orderly bo^ of Captain Helsham's company of Militia for the day mentioned; the initials '^H: P:" stand for Henry Pim, who was Adjutant of the Kilkenny Militia corps of the day. It will be seen by it that the regular garrison duty of the town was then done by the Militia, and there were probably no other soldi^ quartered there at the time : — The post of y* CasUe Quard One Serg* & fifteen men One sentinel! at y* gate^ One sentinell at 8^ Patricks Tower' night & day One sentinell at y* Towne Prison' night <& day — Removed by ord' One sentinell at y* grotto near y* bowling green^ at night Water GaU Po^ One serg^ & fifteen men One sentinell at y* gate Two sentinells at S^ ffrancis Abby at night & one att day One sentinell at Jonas's Tower* oay & night Si Johns GaW Post One Corp^^ & six men One sentinell at y* gate day & night The usual guard in Irishtowne besides Rec* this ord' from y* Towne Maj' y 20**» may 1691 H:P: The following is another list of Captain Helsham's company, but also supplying the names and trades, or occupation, of the im- iThe Castle gate, one of the ports of the city, situate dose to the southern tower of Kilkenny Castle. > The tower over St. Fatrick^s gate. ' The prison of the city was then .situate in Hi^-street, with its rere to Pudding and rennefather lanes. 4 The Bowling-green was in the Cas- tle grounds, immediately adjoining the court-yard — See "Transactions, vol. ii. p. 330. * The position of this eate was on the brid^ over the Bre^acn stream, con-* nectmg Irishtown with the city. The locality is still called Water-gate, but anciently it was known as " the High- town gate." ^ Jonas's tower, also known as Eil- berry tower, and, by a modem corrup- tion, "Tilberry fort," was a flanker of the town wall, situate at the top of Eyans'-lane, and only remoyed within the last fifteen years. 7 The outer gate of St. John's was situate at the east side of the small bridge oyer the mill-stream in John- street. There stood also a gate and tower on St. John's Bridge. 254 fortunateB on whom thej were quartered. The only IVotestant that I can recognifie amon^t the victims is Richard Inwood ; but as he was an ini^eeper it is probable that those licensed to keep houses of entertainment were liable to have Militiar-men billeted upon them, no matter what may have been their religious profession. It will be obserred that Inwood himself served in the Militia, and had his quarters assigned to him elsewhere :— A list of Cap" Jwthua HdBhcma Company June 19» 1691 Joshua Hdsham Cap*^ "j Greorge Burch Lieu^ s Hen : Pjrm Adju^ Bray Beavor Ensigne J MENS* NAMES. QUARTERS. Serg* Pieroe Shortall Malst*^ Rob: Walsh Tan' James Byan Curri' Mrs. Gaffney Bob* Smith 1 f John Meagher skin' Bog' Bragg > Corp^ < Nich : Loughlan brogmak' Richard Rutlan John Bibby £dm<^ Connell } Tho: Heape J I Den: Newman skinn' Tho: Edmonds \ yx„,„ / Tho: Troy Tan' Pet' Burt J I Widdow Marshall Pickerin Ajrey Rich^ Gafney gent W"»Adkin8on Val : Travers Dy' Pet' Archdeacon Barn : Murphey Nich: Bibby Jam: Slattery Tabacon"* W"" Bennett Jam: Shea gent W"" Barton Tho: Ronan Merchant {Edmond Walsh brogmak' Nidi^'^Tnan merch* Thady fiinn Tann' Rich Browne \ Rkh^ Comerford Cottf T^i,« Uo^u^ / Math: ffanning gent JohnBayley | ^^^. j^^ La^Imty Rog' Beard Miles Lyons Brew' Anth: Burt Tho: CodsT MU' {Jam: Meagn' Joh: Hennesy Jam : Maly glov' ^ rn' A I Panl Molloy Curi' ^fi^ ^""^ \ Tho: Phillips joyn' Joh: Lannan W" Kenny glov' Arth' Bates | W" Berry P John Bishop of Keatings toune, 1 Josh: Brennan \ Watts Wall, and Thome back j 255 MEMS* NAIOS. QUARTBRS. r W" Butler skin' '^^*"^®^*^ 1 Derby Brophy CM- : L Jam: Boulger {Tho: Creemill' Jam : Brazell hat' r Joh: Uniack gent Hen: Bnrnside ^ T